# The MATLAB reference files have a SHA-256 recorded in NOTICE, and that digest
# is over the bytes on disk. Git's autocrlf is on by default on Windows, so
# without this line a fresh Windows clone would check them out with CRLF, every
# recorded checksum would fail to reproduce, and the provenance claim in NOTICE
# would look false. -text means: store and check out these bytes unchanged,
# on every platform.
matlab/*.m -text

# Same reasoning, lesser stakes: the generated engine and the provenance
# manifest are diffed byte-for-byte by CI against a fresh `python
# assemble_sicopr.py`. Leaving their line endings to the platform makes that
# diff depend on who ran it.
sicopr.py -text
com_functions/inlined_copies.json -text
